{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2150-05-19 21:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello Mr. ___, I'm Dr. ___. You came in tonight with shortness of breath. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2150-05-19 21:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, doctor. I’ve been feeling more winded over the past few days, especially when walking. I had a cough with some brownish sputum, but that’s mostly gone now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2150-05-19 21:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any fever, chest pain, or swelling in your legs?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2150-05-19 21:18:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No fever or chest pain. Just tired and not sleeping well because of the breathing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2150-05-19 21:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs show your kidney function is worse than before—creatinine is 4.6, up from 1.2. We also found your calcium is very high at 15. That can cause fatigue and confusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2150-05-19 21:20:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "High calcium? But I’ve been drinking okay… maybe not as much as usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2150-05-19 21:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Even small decreases in fluid intake can affect you, especially with your multiple myeloma. We think the high calcium and dehydration are stressing your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2150-05-19 21:22:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh… and my INR is 16? That’s way too high. I’ve been on Coumadin for years."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2150-05-19 21:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s very elevated. It increases your bleeding risk. We gave you plasma and vitamin K to reverse it. We’ll restart Coumadin once we’re sure it’s safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2150-05-19 21:24:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. What about my breathing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2150-05-19 21:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chest X-ray is clearer than last time, but we’re treating you with antibiotics just in case—vancomycin, cefepime, and azithromycin—for possible infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2150-05-19 21:26:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had pneumonia not long ago. I didn’t think it came back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2150-05-19 21:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re being cautious. Your CT scan shows improvement in lung inflammation, so it may not be active infection. But we’ll finish the course."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2150-05-20 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your urine test shows Enterococcus—this is a urinary tract infection. We’ll continue antibiotics that cover it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2150-05-20 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t have burning or urgency. Just less urine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2150-05-20 08:03:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "With your bladder surgery history, symptoms can be subtle. The bacteria count is high, so we treat it even without classic signs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2150-05-20 08:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. How’s my calcium?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2150-05-20 08:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re treating it with IV fluids, steroids, calcitonin, and a medication called pamidronate. It’s starting to come down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2150-05-21 07:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your calcium dropped quickly—now it’s low. We’re giving IV and oral calcium and vitamin D. This can happen after pamidronate, especially with kidney issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2150-05-21 07:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So now it’s too low? I feel okay, just tired."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2150-05-21 07:48:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we’ll keep replacing it. Your parathyroid hormone is high, which means your body is trying to fix it. No sign of a new problem there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2150-05-21 07:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Should I worry about that spine finding on the CT?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2150-05-21 07:51:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "There’s a new slight compression in your mid-back, probably T7. Could be from myeloma, but also from old fractures. We’ll follow up with your oncologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2150-05-21 07:53:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had back pain for years. It hasn’t gotten worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2150-05-21 07:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll monitor it. For now, focus is on your kidneys, calcium, and infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2150-05-22 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your kidney function is improving—creatinine is down to 1.1. That’s back to your baseline. IV fluids helped a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2150-05-22 08:11:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Can I stop the IV fluids?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2150-05-22 08:12:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll taper them. Your urine output is good, and ultrasound showed no blockage—so kidneys are clearing on their own."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2150-05-22 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my INR? Is it safe to restart Coumadin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2150-05-22 08:15:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "INR is now 1.8. We’ve restarted Coumadin at a lower dose. We’ll adjust based on next check."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2150-05-23 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your breathing is better, and the antibiotics are done. CT shows your lungs are mostly clear—just some residual thickening from old COPD."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2150-05-23 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel less short of breath. Still a little tired."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2150-05-23 08:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. Your multiple myeloma markers are improving. We restarted Revlimid at a lower dose and increased it as your kidneys recovered."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2150-05-23 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I stopped it when I got sick. Glad it’s back on track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2150-05-24 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your calcium is stable but still low—around 7.2. You’ll need oral calcium and vitamin D at home. Check levels in two days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2150-05-24 08:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll take the supplements. Any reason it’s not coming up faster?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2150-05-24 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Pamidronate can suppress bone release of calcium for days. Since your kidneys were slow to clear it, the effect lasted longer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2150-05-24 08:19:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Ah, that explains it. What about the gas in my kidney on the CT?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2150-05-24 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s likely from your reconstructed bladder or catheter. No signs of infection, so we’re not treating it. But call if you develop fever or pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2150-05-25 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re planning discharge tomorrow if labs stay stable. You’ll finish the Revlimid cycle at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2150-05-25 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What meds will I be on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2150-05-25 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Same as before, except we’re stopping aspirin—you’re on Coumadin, so you don’t need both. And we’re adding calcium and vitamin D."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2150-05-25 08:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was on aspirin for my heart. Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2150-05-25 08:05:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, Coumadin is stronger for your atrial fibrillation. Aspirin just adds bleeding risk. We’ll restart your metoprolol too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2150-05-26 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set for discharge today. Your breathing is good, kidneys are normal, and infection is treated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2150-05-26 08:11:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel much better. Just need to keep up with the calcium."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2150-05-26 08:12:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Take calcium three times a day and vitamin D twice daily. Check with your pharmacy if you have questions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2150-05-26 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2150-05-26 08:15:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Blood tests tomorrow and in three days for calcium and kidney function. See your oncologist and anticoagulation clinic next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2150-05-26 08:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2150-05-27 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in—how are you feeling at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2150-05-27 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doing okay. Took the calcium like prescribed. No cramps or tingling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2150-05-27 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Keep monitoring. Call if you feel confused, have muscle spasms, or new back pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2150-05-28 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your latest labs show calcium improving—now 8.0. Kidneys still stable. Keep up the good work."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2150-05-28 08:46:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried it wouldn’t come up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2150-05-28 08:47:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It takes time. Continue the supplements and follow up with your oncologist about the spine and myeloma."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2150-05-29 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One more check-in. Any new symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2150-05-29 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, just the usual back ache. Feet still tingle a bit—neuropathy from chemo."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2150-05-29 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s common. Report any worsening. Otherwise, you’re doing well post-hospital."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2150-05-29 09:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks for all the follow-up. I feel lucky to be home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2150-05-30 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final call—your PTHrp result came back negative. So your high calcium wasn’t from a new tumor signal. It was from myeloma activity."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2150-05-30 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know. So it was just the myeloma flaring up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2150-05-30 10:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and dehydration made it worse. Keep up with fluids and meds. See you in clinic soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2150-05-30 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2150-05-31 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Wanted to confirm—you’re officially discharged as of today. All goals met during your stay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2150-05-31 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’m home and doing well. Appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2150-05-31 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Stay hydrated, take your meds, and keep following up. We’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2150-05-31 08:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2150-05-31 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your echocardiogram showed mild pulmonary hypertension and a dilated aorta. Nothing urgent, but your cardiologist should monitor it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2150-05-31 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had heart issues before. I’ll mention it at my next visit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2150-05-31 10:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, just routine follow-up. Otherwise, you’ve recovered well from this admission."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2150-05-31 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel much stronger. Glad it’s behind me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2150-05-31 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming—did you get your prescriptions filled?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2150-05-31 12:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, all done. Calcium, vitamin D, and the rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2150-05-31 12:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Call if you have side effects or questions. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2150-05-31 12:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2150-05-31 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final follow-up: your urine culture later showed normal bacteria—likely contamination. No need for more antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2150-05-31 14:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good to know. I was wondering about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2150-05-31 14:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the Enterococcus was real and treated. The second result isn’t concerning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2150-05-31 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks for clarifying."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2150-05-31 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last check—how’s your energy?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2150-05-31 16:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. Still tired, but not like in the hospital."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2150-05-31 16:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. Rest and stay consistent with your care. We’ll see you in clinic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2150-05-31 16:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2150-05-31 16:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care and stay well."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2150-05-19 21:03:00",
    "admission_end": "2150-05-31 18:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted with worsening dyspnea, found to have acute renal failure, hypercalcemia, and an elevated INR of 16. The hypercalcemia, secondary to multiple myeloma progression, was treated with IV fluids, pamidronate, calcitonin, and steroids, leading to subsequent hypocalcemia managed with aggressive calcium and vitamin D repletion. His renal function improved with hydration, and Coumadin was held then restarted after INR normalization with FFP and vitamin K. A urinary tract infection with Enterococcus was treated with antibiotics. His respiratory symptoms resolved with a course of vancomycin, cefepime, and azithromycin, supported by improving CT findings. Revlimid was resumed as renal function recovered. He was discharged home ambulatory with plans for close outpatient follow-up for calcium monitoring, oncology care, and anticoagulation management.",
    "problems": [
      "Hypercalcemia",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Multiple myeloma, without mention of having achieved remission",
      "Urinary tract infection, site not specified",
      "Abnormal coagulation profile",
      "Hypocalcemia",
      "Chronic airway obstruction, not elsewhere classified",
      "Atrial fibrillation",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of native coronary artery",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified"
    ]
  }
}
